00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:01,960
Okay, first question, is a ketogenic diet appropriate

00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,560
for every cancer patient?

00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,920
So if you've been with me long enough,

00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,280
you know the answer to that is no.

00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:12,280
So in general, though, doing a keto-like type diet

00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:17,640
would be, I guess, appropriate for every person, period,

00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:18,920
not even cancer.

00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,160
You don't want to be eating a lot of sugar.

00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,000
So when you're eating a ton of carbs,

00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,680
I know there are carbohydrates,

00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,560
the halux, carbohydrates, you know,

00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:30,280
root deterians, all this kind of stuff out there

00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:32,760
in the world and you could find some YouTube videos

00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:37,440
on people that only eat grains or I don't know.

00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:40,840
I just don't know that that's how we were mentally

00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:45,200
and certainly people that are vegetarians

00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,960
are certainly eating a lot more carbohydrates in general too.

00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:54,960
So but I would suggest that it would probably be

00:01:55,280 --> 00:02:00,080
in the best interest of most people of the planet

00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:02,080
to be eating less carbohydrates.

00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,360
Certainly most people in the United States

00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:08,360
since we have been a pharmacolic nation for a long time.

00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,720
So eating the more of a keto-like diet,

00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:15,160
to think that keto diet is technically getting in ketosis,

00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,560
to think that we all need to be in ketosis

00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,680
is I think very incorrect.

00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,920
Our cells are made to feed off of glucose

00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,240
and that's how we produce energy.

00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,280
But for a cancer patient,

00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,480
to never cancer patient be on a ketogenic diet.

00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,800
No, I don't think so either,

00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,560
but again, eating more keto-like would be more appropriate.

00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,080
Next question, we have another keto question.

00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,720
I'm doing keto.

00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:46,040
It's tempting to buy plant-based dairy products

00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,920
to take the place of real dairy,

00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:51,960
such as cream cheese, cheese, yogurt, et cetera.

00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:56,600
But looking at these ingredients in these plant-based substitutes,

00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:01,600
they look a little bit like fracon foods, isolates, gums, et cetera.

00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:06,120
Is it better to void these altogether

00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:10,640
or are all these additives relatively harmless?

00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:14,840
Well, I would say some are relatively harmless,

00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:19,840
some of the gums and some of the other different substitutes

00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,600
that they use.

00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,080
You can develop antibodies against it

00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,560
so that you could have sensitivities to it.

00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:33,520
But some of the fibers and stuff that they use

00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,800
are relatively harmless.

00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,800
You'd have to look up each ingredient.

00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:42,120
Obviously, it's much better to eat real dairy,

00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,840
but we're trying to stay up here on a dairy-free diet.

00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,480
You can't do that.

00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,760
So just stay away from some of those things

00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,320
are probably the best.

00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:54,640
As far as yogurt, like there's coconut milk,

00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:57,440
yogurt's out there that I think are just fine.

00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:03,720
Most of the dairy yogurt that you find out there

00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:06,160
unless you're getting it organic

00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,200
has got a bunch of additives and garbage.

00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,880
Most of the dairy products,

00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:13,920
unless you're getting it clean, dairy, clean, organic

00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,440
or from the farm or something like that,

00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:20,280
it's gonna have a bunch of garbage in it as well.

00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:25,280
So just because it's dairy doesn't mean that

00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:30,480
it's necessarily going to be good for us either.

00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:35,480
So there's a lot of nasty stuff even in

00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,440
what we would term as real food as well.

00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:44,000
So next question.

00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,240
Don't tumors continuously shed cancer cells?

00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,440
I think they're talking about tumor cells.

00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:53,640
They're shedding circulated tumor cells.

00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:58,640
It's hard to imagine that they do that and fits and spurs,

00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,440
but maybe they do.

00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:09,920
I think it's hard to imagine that tumors

00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:14,920
will release circulated tumor cells in pulses or spurs,

00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,880
but maybe they do.

00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:20,200
But if they shed continuously,

00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:24,560
then why would anyone ever have zero circulated tumor cells

00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,880
if they do have a tumor?

00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:31,880
Even if some have moved on to tissue or to the liver

00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,760
there shouldn't still be some in the blood

00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:38,680
if there be a continuously shed, no?

00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:44,920
Well, there's no data that tells us how

00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:49,760
and when growing tumors will most likely

00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:53,120
be releasing circulated tumor cells.

00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:58,120
I have said over the years that I don't put a lot of faith

00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:01,840
in the circulated tumor cell test

00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:06,840
because I have just seen through my patient based,

00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:10,760
patients that have done the circulated tumor cell test

00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:14,160
have come back with elevated circulated tumor cells

00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:18,200
but no other evidence of cancer growth

00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:21,480
or the opposite, they've come back with no circulated

00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:25,320
tumor cell evidence in the test

00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:29,560
and yet have all sorts of other evidence of tumor growth.

00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:32,160
So given that data,

00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:35,560
then I would say that for someone

00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,920
to have zero circulated tumor cells in the blood

00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:42,480
is not a typically valid test to say

00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:45,840
that the person doesn't have any cancer growth

00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,680
or the cancer is dead or the cancer is walled off.

00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,560
Again, like any lab that you do,

00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:58,560
any lab has variables and any lab is there to give you clues.

00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,120
It gives you ideas, nothing's gonna be perfect.

00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,600
I'm gonna do this test and this is gonna tell me

00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:06,040
if I'm cancer-free or this is gonna tell me

00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:09,000
if my cancer is growing like crazy.

00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,240
None of that one test is gonna be perfect in that scenario.

00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:15,920
Even your gold standard PET scan,

00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:20,240
you could have a very rapidly growing new tumor

00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:23,400
that is metastasized in your liver, let's say,

00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:27,400
but it's still only two million cells large

00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,320
and it's not picked up by the PET scan

00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:32,720
so you could be given a no evidence of disease

00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:36,160
from your oncologist and yet you have a lot of evidence

00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,960
of disease, you have a lot of disease,

00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:41,240
they just haven't found the evidence yet.

00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:44,720
So that's why they term it that way.

00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:47,280
The test doesn't show that there's cancer,

00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:49,920
it doesn't mean that there's not cancer.

00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:53,080
And likewise, you could have something light up on a PET scan

00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:55,560
and yet it was just metabolically active

00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,840
at that time of the PET scan.

00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,200
It's not really actively growing.

00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,800
That's why you wanna compare with other previous test.

00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,960
If you have a previous PET scan to see,

00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,880
okay, let's look at the size.

00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,880
Well, it is metabolically active in the lung here,

00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:12,240
but it's actually smaller than it was before

00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:14,440
or it's much larger than it was before.

00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:17,200
So you're getting these clues from these tests

00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,920
and you look at other labs.

00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:22,040
Well, has this, as the alkaline phosphatase going up,

00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:25,160
has the calcium levels going up, is it?

00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:27,960
So no test, I know we all want.

00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:31,400
I just want to run this test and know exactly where I'm at.

00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:34,200
Well, I could lie to you.

00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,800
I mean, oncologists tend to do that a lot.

00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,120
They just tell you what you want to hear,

00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,800
but that's not true.

00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:43,960
So I just want to be giving you real data

00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,640
that is not as possible.

00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:48,720
None of these tests are gonna be perfect.

00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,760
None of these tests can just call my heart

00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,440
that we're all okay.

00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,920
There are none of these tests should cause us to freak out

00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,560
because we just don't know the full story.

00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:00,120
And we're not at that place in modern medicine

00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:03,280
yet that is gonna give us that full data yet.

00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:07,280
So you have to use differential diagnosis

00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:09,440
and use as much data as you possibly can

00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,680
to come to the best conclusion,

00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:15,440
to make a decision whether you should change treatment.

00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,560
And to what degree you should change the treatment

00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,880
that you're already doing.

00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:26,080
So sometimes I think that, you know,

00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,720
I know as humans we want to know

00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,920
that everything is black and white

00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:33,080
is my tumor turned on, there's a turned off.

00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:36,280
I just need to know and we need to know this data.

00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:40,400
And I know that some of us are more analytical

00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:43,680
and more linear than others than we want

00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,680
to have this information

00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:50,440
because it really helps us in our decision-making process.

00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,800
And I'm like that, that's me.

00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:56,920
And the more you learn, the more you learn

00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:59,440
that that's just not what life is like.

00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:02,960
And I think that sometimes God doesn't allow it

00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:05,840
to be like that because it forces us

00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:09,440
to do either dependent upon who we're gonna put,

00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,800
who are we gonna put our faith in?

00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,640
You know where we're gonna put our faith in the tester?

00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,040
We're gonna put our faith in the treatment

00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:16,640
or we're gonna put our faith in the Lord Jesus

00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:20,160
and our Heavenly Father that He's gonna guide us.

00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:22,600
So during difficult times of our life,

00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,720
whether it's cancer or it's financial issues

00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:28,320
or it's a death of the family, it has to,

00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,200
we have to let those things drive us

00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:34,280
to a deeper relationship with Him

00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:39,040
so that we can have that intimacy with our Heavenly Father

00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:43,280
and that dependence upon that relationship.

00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:47,720
So we can have peace in whatever decision that we're making.

00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,920
And I know, oh, that's two of two.

00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
So I just don't want that.

00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,200
I want to get the science.

00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,720
I want the data.

00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:56,240
Well, that's just not what life is about.

00:10:56,240 --> 00:11:00,840
So there's nothing wrong with seeking information.

00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:04,000
There's nothing wrong with learning as much as you possibly can

00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,680
but it all ends up bouncing back to,

00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,520
we have to depend on the Lord.

00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:13,400
I'm gonna get as much data as I possibly can.

00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,560
Knowing that science is imperfect

00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:18,040
and it's changing on a daily basis.

00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:21,200
And then I have to ultimately fall back

00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,560
on my relationship with Him

00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:26,640
and depend on Him for my answers.

00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,000
Okay, next question.

00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:32,880
Researching the curcumin in raw tumeric,

00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,760
it turns out that there's only between three

00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:40,760
and 10% of curcumin in raw tumeric root.

00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:45,680
So I understand curcumin is considered to be the active form

00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,200
of the tumeric.

00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:52,720
In tumeric, so tumeric is the root.

00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:56,920
Curcumin is a curcuminoid that's in the,

00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,160
in the plant, in the plant.

00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,160
And that's the thing that studied

00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,720
is the separated curcuminoids

00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:06,560
in a lot of the studies that are out there.

00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:09,160
So when you see curcumin helps kill cancer

00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:12,080
or curcumin helps decrease inflammation,

00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:16,120
most of the studies are done with the curcumin.

00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:19,120
They're the most cure form of curcumin,

00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:23,920
typically the 95% curcuminoids products that are out there.

00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,880
So next part of this question.

00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,120
In looking at supplements,

00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:32,360
some of them say standardized to 95% curcuminoids.

00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,960
So with this mean that if the supplement contains

00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:39,320
let's say a thousand milligrams of tumeric

00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,480
that somehow they've concentrated the curcumin

00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:46,480
in the product that there's probably 950 milligrams

00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:50,320
of curcumin, I believe that's what it means.

00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:53,200
But here's the caveat on that.

00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:59,520
So most of the studies that are done on supplements,

00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,800
like I said with curcumin are,

00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,080
is the separated curcumin.

00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:08,240
But there's more, more data out there

00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,200
that isn't basically included in studies

00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,480
that the whole food of the product

00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:17,080
may actually have more value

00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:20,480
than the curcuminoid portion.

00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,400
So you can't argue with, okay,

00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,760
X amount of grams of curcuminoids

00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:27,640
have decreased tumer growth, et cetera.

00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,640
But does that mean that you shouldn't use

00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,880
the whole form of tumeric?

00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:36,440
So I am a fan of whole food

00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,600
philosophy,

00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:44,080
meaning that the way God created tumeric

00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:48,800
with all the other curcuminoids that are in it

00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:51,920
and all the other cofactors and phenols

00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,800
and alkaloids that are in the tumeric

00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:58,440
can actually have a synergistic relationship

00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:02,000
and actually help the curcumin that is in it

00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,480
actually function better.

00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:09,480
So I know when this person wrote this question

00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:12,360
because we had spoken the other day

00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:16,920
and we talked about, she uses raw tumeric root,

00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:20,280
grown up and basically she doesn't juice it

00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:23,400
but she's blending it into a smoothie

00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,120
and I told her I thought that was a better idea

00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:30,280
but you could search for how many grams of curcumin

00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:34,400
are in the tumeric root and she did so

00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:39,280
and she saw that only about 10% of curcumin,

00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:43,640
there's only about 10% of curcumin in a raw tumeric.

00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:47,200
So if you have 10 grams of raw tumeric

00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:52,120
you're only gonna get about one gram of curcumin.

00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:55,360
Now that is probably true, I'm not doubting that

00:14:55,360 --> 00:15:00,360
but we can't forget that there's synergistic benefits

00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,600
of the whole food.

00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:07,600
So I would recommend that you continue your practice

00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:13,600
of using turmeric and I would bet

00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:18,440
if you had a kitchen scale and you weighed your raw tumeric root

00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:22,360
that you could get, I don't know how many grams

00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:25,680
you could get in your serving that you're blending

00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:29,480
in your drink but if you got 10 grams

00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:34,040
in your drink you may only be getting one gram

00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:38,240
of pure curcumin but it's a synergistic effects of that

00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:41,680
that it actually may function as six or seven grams

00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:44,080
of curcumin in your body.

